## Summary

Coordinated alignment with sinfactura/api. The sinfactura/app FE was out of sync on both feature-key vocabulary and the `SubscriptionSyncPayload` shape; this update makes the types match what `GET /subscription` actually returns on the wire.

Companion PR in sinfactura/app updates the slice + reducer + all callsites to consume the new shape.

## Changes

### FeatureKey renames (4)
- `afip` → `afipInvoicing`
- `stripePayments` → `paymentIntegrations`
- `cash` → `cashManagement`
- `reportsAdvanced` → `advancedReports`

### FeatureKey additions (4)
- `whatsappCommerce`, `aiFeatures`, `mobileApp`, `customDomain` — declared even when their epics haven't shipped; matrix can set `enabled:false` until then.

### Entitlement type
- `enabled` widened to `boolean | null` to match the wire format for numeric/metered features (where the gating signal is `limit`, not `enabled`).
- Added optional `source?: 'plan' | 'override' | 'trial'` — the BE always sends it.

### `SubscriptionSyncPayload` replaced with flat shape

Before:
```ts
interface SubscriptionSyncPayload {
  subscription: Subscription;
  entitlements: ResolvedEntitlements;
  usage?: UsageCounters;
}
```

After (matches GET /subscription directly):
```ts
interface SubscriptionSyncPayload {
  planTier: PlanTier;
  status: SubscriptionStatus;
  billingCycle: BillingCycle | null;
  currentPeriodStart: number | null;
  currentPeriodEnd: number | null;
  trialEndsAt: number | null;
  freeUntil?: string;
  cancelAt: number | null;
  canceledAt: number | null;
  entitlements: SubscriptionEntitlementEntry[];
  usage: SubscriptionUsageEntry[];
}
```

`Subscription`, `UsageCounters`, `ResolvedEntitlements` are unchanged — they remain as the resolved / canonical internal shapes that the FE slice converts the wire format into.

### Auxiliary types
- `SubscriptionEntitlementEntry` — per-array element shape returned by BE.
- `SubscriptionUsageEntry` — per-array element shape returned by BE.

## Version

Bumps from 1.1.0 → 1.2.0 (minor — pre-launch we can be liberal with breaking changes; consumers re-pin).

## Breaking changes

Any consumer that imports `SubscriptionSyncPayload` directly or hardcodes the renamed feature keys (`afip`, `stripePayments`, `cash`, `reportsAdvanced`). At time of writing, only sinfactura/app FE consumes these — the companion PR there is in flight.

